error[DZ0502]: `300` does not fit in `u8`
  ┌─ D:/OdinProjects/Dazzle/tests/workspace/typeerrors/src/errors.dz:5:18
  │
5 │     World      = 300
  │                  ^^^ outside the range of `u8`
  │
  = help: valid values are 0 to 255

error[DZ0517]: a struct field cannot hold `&Vec3`
   ┌─ D:/OdinProjects/Dazzle/tests/workspace/typeerrors/src/errors.dz:23:17
   │
23 │     borrowed:   &Vec3
   │                 ^^^^^ references live only on the stack
   │
   = help: use `^T` for a stored pointer — a reference in a field could outlive what it points at, and Dazzle has no lifetimes to catch that (spec §5.2)

error[DZ0507]: cannot assign to `count`
   ┌─ D:/OdinProjects/Dazzle/tests/workspace/typeerrors/src/errors.dz:34:9
   │
34 │         count += 1
   │         ^^^^^ not mutable
   │
   = help: declare it as `let mut count` to allow assignment

error[DZ0501]: expected `i64`, found `i32`
   ┌─ D:/OdinProjects/Dazzle/tests/workspace/typeerrors/src/errors.dz:39:12
   │
39 │     return small
   │            ^^^^^ this is `i32`
   │
   = help: Dazzle has no implicit numeric conversions, not even widening (spec §5.1) — write `... as i64`

